{"The Zod schema uses computed keys via [z.string().toString()] which does not behave like an index signature and won't validate responses as intended - should use z.record(...) or .passthrough() instead": 0.9416810870170593, "refreshOAuthTokens can return a fetch Response when credential syncing is enabled, but callers expect different shapes (axios responses with .data, or provider SDK token objects), which can break token refresh flows at runtime": 0.9459096789360046, "The secret comparison for the webhook endpoint should properly handle string | string[] header values": 0.849373996257782, "The webhook endpoint should use constant-time compare for secret validation": 0.7136698365211487, "The webhook endpoint needs abuse protections including method restriction, size limits, rate limiting, and replay protection since it can overwrite credentials if the secret leaks": 0.8294124007225037, "The schema needs to explicitly model expires_in/expiry_date and refresh_token handling": 0.6872786283493042, "The webhook handler lacks request method validation": 0.8724331855773926, "The webhook handler doesn't normalize header value types (string vs string[])": 0.6992063522338867, "The webhook handler doesn't wrap decrypt/JSON parsing in try/catch - bad payload or missing/invalid CALCOM_APP_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY can throw and return 500 instead of clear 4xx errors": 0.9273245930671692}